# Wail of the Forgotten (Descend 8): "Choose one. If there are eight or more permanent cards in your graveyard as you cast this spell,
# choose one or more instead" (CR 700.2, 207.2c, 110.4a). Turn 1: two Thought Scours mill four Grizzly Bears into Bot1's graveyard. Turn 3: Bot2's
# graveyard holds a Forest (discarded to hand size), which is not Bot1's: Black Lotus sacrificed for mana makes five permanent cards and a third
# Scour mills two Hill Giants, seven in all. With seven, two modes (and three) are refused as Wail is cast, one is chosen: it returns Bot1's own
# Mox Jet to hand (a land is no target, CR 115.1; Wail the sorcery is no permanent card). Turn 5: a fourth Scour mills a Hill Giant and a
# Lightning Bolt, so eight permanent cards (Bot1's Wail the sorcery is not one, nor the Scours, nor the Bolt): all three modes are chosen. The opponent's
# Ornithopter goes to its hand (mode 1, an opponent's permanent), Bot2 (a player who is not Bot1) discards (mode 2), and Bot1 looks at its
# top three cards, takes the Lightning Bolt and puts the Ornithopter and the Grizzly Bears into its graveyard (mode 3).

